  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE (pending build verification): negative-binomial series generalization formalized as thin wrappers over Mathlib + 2 genuine derivations; 8 theorems, 0 axioms, 0 sorries.",
    "builtItems": [
      "GeometricSeriesOQ06OQ02.hasSum_choose_mul_geometric / summable_ / tsum_ (Part I): named HasSum/Summable/tsum wrappers for the k-indexed family",
      "tsum_geometric_of_negBinom (k=0), tsum_succ_mul_geometric (k=1) anchoring specializations",
      "tsum_coe_mul_geometric_from_negBinom: parent recovery ∑ n·rⁿ = r/(1-r)² as (k=1)-(k=0)",
      "tsum_descFactorial_mul_geometric: descending-factorial form k!/(1-r)^(k+1)",
      "tsum_choose_two_half_pow: concrete ∑ binom(n+2,2)·(1/2)ⁿ = 8"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "The k-fold term-by-term derivative (÷ k!) of ∑ rⁿ = 1/(1-r) is exactly the negative-binomial series ∑ binom(n+k,k)·rⁿ = 1/(1-r)^(k+1) for ‖r‖<1.",
      "Mathlib already packages the full family as hasSum_choose_mul_geometric_of_norm_lt_one (Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Normed, line 468), stated over a NormedDivisionRing 𝕜; NormedField suffices since it extends NormedDivisionRing and auto-provides HasSummableGeomSeries (instance at line 368).",
      "The parent arithmetico-geometric first moment ∑ n·rⁿ = r/(1-r)² is recovered cleanly as the (k=1) family minus the (k=0) geometric series via HasSum.sub, exhibiting the parent as a special case.",
      "Descending-factorial reformulation ∑ (n+k) descFactorial k · rⁿ = k!/(1-r)^(k+1) follows by rescaling binom by k! using Nat.descFactorial_eq_factorial_mul_choose."
    ],
